{"task_id": "Mbpp/56", "solution": "def check(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given non-negative integer is one less than twice its reverse.\n    The reverse operation considers decimal digits, dropping leading zeros.\n    \"\"\"\n    original_n = n\n    \n    # Calculate the reverse of n using arithmetic\n    reversed_n = 0\n    temp_n = n\n    if temp_n == 0: # Handle the special case for 0 explicitly as the loop condition is > 0\n        reversed_n = 0\n    else:\n        while temp_n > 0:\n            digit = temp_n % 10\n            reversed_n = reversed_n * 10 + digit\n            temp_n //= 10\n    \n    # Calculate the value: 2 * reverse(n) - 1\n    computed_value = 2 * reversed_n - 1\n    \n    # Compare with the original number\n    return original_n == computed_value"}
