{"task_id": "Mbpp/142", "solution": "def count_samepair(l1, l2, l3):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts items that are identical at the same position across three lists.\n    Compares elements at each index up to the minimum length of the lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = min(len(l1), len(l2), len(l3))\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        try:\n            if l1[i] == l2[i] == l3[i]:\n                count += 1\n        except Exception:\n            # Treat any comparison error (e.g., incomparable types) as non-equal.\n            continue\n    return count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/145", "solution": "def max_Abs_Diff(seq):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum difference between any two elements in a given sequence.\n    It performs a single pass to find the minimum and maximum values.\n    \"\"\"\n    iterator = iter(seq)\n    first = float(next(iterator))\n    min_val = max_val = first\n\n    for v in iterator:\n        fv = float(v)\n        if fv < min_val:\n            min_val = fv\n        elif fv > max_val:\n            max_val = fv\n\n    return float(max_val - min_val)"}
