{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "import math\n\ndef next_Perfect_Square(n: float) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the smallest perfect square strictly greater than the given number n.\n    Handles both positive and negative input values.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        return 0\n    \n    # Find the integer floor of the square root of n.\n    # For n=35, r_candidate = floor(sqrt(35)) = floor(5.916) = 5\n    # For n=36, r_candidate = floor(sqrt(36)) = floor(6.0) = 6\n    r_candidate = int(math.floor(math.sqrt(n)))\n    \n    # If r_candidate squared is less than or equal to n, we need the next integer root.\n    # This ensures the result is *strictly* greater than n.\n    # For n=35, 5*5 = 25 <= 35, so r = 6\n    # For n=36, 6*6 = 36 <= 36, so r = 7\n    if (r_candidate * r_candidate) <= n:\n        r_candidate += 1\n        \n    return r_candidate * r_candidate"}
