{"task_id": "Mbpp/462", "solution": "from typing import List, TypeVar\n\nT = TypeVar(\"T\")\n\ndef combinations_list(items: List[T]) -> List[List[T]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds all possible combinations (power set) of the elements of a given list.\n    Elements in each combination are ordered by their original index in descending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(items)\n    result: List[List[T]] = []\n\n    # Iterate through all possible masks from 0 to 2^n - 1\n    for mask in range(1 << n):\n        subset: List[T] = []\n        # Build the subset based on the current mask, adding elements in descending index order\n        for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n            if (mask >> i) & 1:  # Check if the i-th bit of the mask is set\n                subset.append(items[i])\n        result.append(subset)\n    return result"}
